## BUYER INTENT
- deal_readiness = Cold / Warm / Hot — the buyer's readiness TEMPERATURE, rolled up from call lead-tags + live engagement (Hot ≈ ready-to-buy now, Cold ≈ just browsing). Emit ONLY when a call/PNS lead-tag or a clear live signal supports it; OMIT otherwise. Policy: INTENT.
- use_case = WHY the buyer needs the product — the stated application / end-use (e.g. 'raw material to manufacture notebooks', 'fleet for last-mile delivery'). From ISQ buyerInfo when filled, else a grounded read of the requirement + calls; NEVER invent one. Emit ONLY on an explicit use/application signal; OMIT otherwise. Policy: PROCUREMENT.
- buyer_intent = current purchasing SERIOUSNESS + STAGE as one read (Low / Medium / High + Browsing / Comparing / Ready-to-buy) from LIVE signals only; old leads are past demand, not low intent. Source priority: PNS seriousness + callback-urgency > recent CSL > live WhatsApp > recent BuyLeads.

## COMMUNICATION
- communication = preferred channel + responsiveness + language as one (e.g. 'Phone+WhatsApp · selective · Hindi'). Responsiveness grounded in REAL two-way behaviour (one-tap auto-replies / a low campaign response-rate are NOT responsive — say 'selective' + cite the rate). Language ONLY from a buyer-authored signal (never our Hindi campaigns or auto-generated enquiry text), else OMIT language. Source priority: genuine two-way BUYER turns (WHATSAPP / PNS) for responsiveness; a buyer-authored signal for language.

## LOCATION
- location_sourcing_preference = the buyer's operating city + every distinct city they SOURCE-FROM; emit BOTH when they differ (e.g. 'Operates in East Delhi · Sources from Kanpur, Mumbai') and never collapse multiple sourcing cities. Source priority: verified GST / Udyam / Befisc registered-address city (for operating) > per-call buyer city > BuyLead search-city / PNS seller-city (sourcing only).
