  VERIFIED-ADDRESS LOCK: a verified GST / Udyam / Befisc address that names the SAME city as the registered profile city CONFIRMS it — keep it, do NOT flip, even when PNS mentions another city; 'near the seller' can never override two agreeing address sources; and PNS buyer_locations / seller_locations are AGGREGATE arrays pooled across ALL calls (they blend the buyer's visit cities, near-seller proximity, and the sellers' own cities) — a city in buyer_locations is NOT a reliable per-call operating address, treat every city in them as a SOURCING / proximity hint at most, and it can NEVER override the verified-address lock.
  OUR-OUTBOUND IS NEVER A SOURCING SIGNAL: a city that appears ONLY inside an OUR-outbound line must NOT populate 'Sources from'; and NEVER echo the buyer's own registered / operating city back as a 'sources from' city (circular).
  PAN-ONLY SPECIAL CASE : when there is NO verified operating anchor at all (no GST / Udyam registered-address city, no per-call buyer city, no explicit 'my shop / unit is in X' statement) — for example a person with only a PAN — the registered profile city is a STRONG anchor: KEEP it as the operating city and NEVER promote a browse / telecom-circle / BuyLead sourcing city to operating in its place (those become 'Sources from' at most).
