EVIDENCE ROLES — tag EACH source you consider, per attribute (the role is contextual — the same source can be Primary here and Corroborative there):
  Primary (decides the value) · Authoritative (a verified registration that owns the field) · Behavioural (spoken/written buyer behaviour) · Historical (a repeated pattern over time) · Interest (browsing/discovery only) · Corroborative (agrees → raises confidence, cannot decide alone) · Supporting (adds explanation, never changes the verdict) · Conflict (disagrees → lowers confidence, list it in contradictions) · Ignored (available but a higher-priority source won — give the reason) · Missing (an expected source was absent → lower confidence).

REQUIREMENTS ARE DYNAMIC: a SINGLE requirement is only SUPPORTING evidence (one RFQ can be mis-classified — a vague title, a wrong category). But >=3 DISTINCT (non-re-search) requirements in the same category cluster spanning >=30 days = PRIMARY historical procurement evidence — trust the repeated pattern. So do not treat "Requirements" as uniformly weak: weak for one lead, strong as a consistent pattern.

CROSS-SOURCE CORROBORATION drives confidence: it is not only "which source is highest" but "which OTHER sources agree". Three independent sources agreeing (e.g. GST=Manufacturer + a repeated Requirement pattern + a PNS "we manufacture") is HIGH confidence because they converge — record them in agreement.agreeing. Sources that disagree go in agreement.conflicting AND contradictions, and LOWER confidence.

